d assess the ways human experiences are represented in texts", "x0": 0.22967032967032966, "y0": 0.26728826728826727, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.2804972804972805}, {"text": "Question 1 (3 marks)", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.3139083139083139, "x1": 0.2956043956043956, "y1": 0.32634032634032634}, {"text": "Text 1 \u2014 Illustration", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.3418803418803419, "x1": 0.29120879120879123, "y1": 0.35120435120435123}, {"text": "How does the composer use visual devices to communicate an idea about imagination? 3", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.3682983682983683, "x1": 0.8549450549450549, "y1": 0.3815073815073815}, {"text": "Section I continues on page 3", "x0": 0.3758241758241758, "y0": 0.8881118881118881, "x1": 0.6230769230769231, "y1": 0.9013209013209014}], [{"text": "Question 2 (4 marks)", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.2956043956043956, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "Text 2\u2014 Poem", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.1250971250971251, "x1": 0.24285714285714285, "y1": 0.13442113442113443}, {"text": "\u2018Analyse how the contrast between life and death is represented by the poet. 4", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.1592851592851593, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.17249417249417248}, {"text": "Section I continues on page 4", "x0": 0.3758241758241758, "y0": 0.804972804972805, "x1": 0.6230769230769231, "y1": 0.8181818181818182}], [{"text": "Question 3 (3 marks)", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.2956043956043956, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "Text 3 \u2014 Discursive extract", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.11810411810411811, "x1": 0.34945054945054943, "y1": 0.12742812742812742}, {"text": "to explore a unique perspective of travel. 3", "x0": 0.5010989010989011, "y0": 0.1452991452991453, "x1": 0.8549450549450549, "y1": 0.1585081585081585}, {"text": "\u2018Analyse how the author uses language dev", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.1452991452991453, "x1": 0.46153846153846156, "y1": 0.1585081585081585}, {"text": "Section I continues on page 5", "x0": 0.3758241758241758, "y0": 0.7622377622377622, "x1": 0.6230769230769231, "y1": 0.7746697746697747}], [{"text": "Question 4 (4 marks)", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.2956043956043956, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "Text 4 \u2014 Prose fiction extracts", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.12432012432012432, "x1": 0.3758241758241758, "y1": 0.13442113442113443}, {"text": "Explain how the image supports the speaker\u2019s emotions in the written extract. 4", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.1592851592851593, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.17249417249417248}, {"text": "Section I continues on pages 6 and 7", "x0": 0.34615384615384615, "y0": 0.8337218337218337, "x1": 0.6538461538461539, "y1": 0.846930846930847}], [{"text": "Question 5 (6 marks)", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.2956043956043956, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "Text 5 \u2014 Persuasive extract", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.12432012432012432, "x1": 0.3516483516483517, "y1": 0.13442113442113443}, {"text": "Discuss how Julia Gillard makes connections with the reader and wider world by using both", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.1592851592851593, "x1": 0.8637362637362638, "y1": 0.17249417249417248}, {"text": "reflective and persuasive devices to represent the courageousness of women. 6", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.17715617715617715, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.19036519036519037}], [{"text": "Question 5 (continued)", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.3054945054945055, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "End of Section I", "x0": 0.4318681318681319, "y0": 0.6868686868686869, "x1": 0.5681318681318681, "y1": 0.696969696969697}], [{"text": "SECTION IL", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08935508935508936, "x1": 0.23186813186813188, "y1": 0.09867909867909867}, {"text": "20 marks", 